  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed with the particle に to mark the activity being enjoyed: ～に{興|きょう}じる. Has a slightly literary or refined tone compared to casual alternatives like {楽|たの}しむ.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Pattern: [activity]に{興|きょう}じる\n- Conjugates as an ichidan verb: {興|きょう}じる → {興|きょう}じて → {興|きょう}じた\n- The variant {興|きょう}ずる (literary/classical) is also seen\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ゲームに{興|きょう}じる: to enjoy games\n- {会話|かいわ}に{興|きょう}じる: to enjoy conversation\n- {遊|あそ}びに{興|きょう}じる: to amuse oneself with play\n- {宴|うたげ}に{興|きょう}じる: to enjoy a banquet",
